# solar-ctl SSH policy: root-only, key-only.
#
# "-B" rejects all password authentication -> only holders of a key in
# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys (installed by the solar-rootkeys recipe) get
# in, and only as root: every other account has no key and no usable
# password. OE's default "-w" would deny root logins entirely.
#
# NOTE: the allow-root-login IMAGE_FEATURE's postcommand seds away "-w"
# lines here; keeping only -B means whatever that does, password auth
# stays off.
DROPBEAR_EXTRA_ARGS="-B"
